      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This bug has existed for years at this point.  It got briefly fixed and then reverted by a hotfix like a week later and never touched again.  The actual cause is something in the audio code bugging out so it can't keep up with where audio sources are meant to come from.  I don't have the exact error message of it in my latest VRChat logs, but you can see a recurring audio engine error plain as day repeating through your logfile once it happens in-game. \n(Hence why changing worlds solves nothing;  The problems fundamentally in the client code itself)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
